TITLE:: Compressor
summary:: a feed forward compressor at audio rate - downward or upward, with a sidechain and an eq on it
categories:: Libraries>Compressor
related:: Classes/FxUnit, Classes/ParaEQ, Classes/FxChain, Classes/CompressorGUI, Classes/CompressorPanel, Classes/Compander

DESCRIPTION::
A dynamics processor with the shape of a modern plugin compressor - threshold,
ratio, soft knee, attack, release, lookahead, range, mix, makeup - and two
things a plugin usually keeps for a bigger brother: an strong::upward:: mode
that lifts what falls under the threshold, and a strong::sidechain:: that
listens through a five band link::Classes/ParaEQ:: of its own. Everything is
audio rate: the gain is a signal, computed sample by sample; nothing here is
link::Classes/Compander::.

The DSP is one pseudo-UGen, link::#*ar::, so it runs wherever a UGen does; and
an instance of this class drives it wherever it runs - see link::Classes/FxUnit::
for the three ways.

code::
s.boot;
Ndef(\bass, { var sig = LFSaw.ar([55, 55.3]) * 0.2; Compressor.ar(sig, \comp) }).play;

c = Compressor(Ndef(\bass), \comp);
c.gui;
c.threshold = -24; c.ratio = 4; c.attack = 0.005; c.release = 0.12;
c.preset = \glue;
::

subsection:: How the gain is worked out

definitionList::
## detector || the sidechain, or the input, through the eq; then either its absolute value or a 5 ms rms; the channels linked towards their loudest by link::#-link::
## computer || the level in dB against link::#-threshold::, through a soft link::#-knee::, at link::#-ratio::; never further than link::#-range::. Downward mode squashes what goes over the threshold; upward mode mirrors this under it, and code::range:: is what keeps silence from being lifted
## ballistics || the gain in dB, smoothed: link::#-attack:: seconds when it moves away from 0 dB, link::#-release:: coming back - as time constants, so 10 ms means what it means on a desk
## lookahead || the signal is held back by up to 20 ms so the gain gets there first
## output || gain plus makeup, mixed with the dry signal by link::#-mix::
::

link::#*staticGain:: is the computer in numbers, so the window's curve is the
curve the server runs. That is the one thing this class has to get right:
change link::#*ar:: and link::#*staticGain:: together.

subsection:: The sidechain

link::#*ar:: takes a signal the detector can listen to instead of the input; the
object says which with link::#-sidechain::. A node of its own reads an external
bus with link::Classes/InFeedback::, so a bus written later in the tree than the
compressor still arrives - a block late, which a sidechain does not mind. Either
way the detector listens through link::#-eq::, a ParaEQ that shapes only what
the detector hears, and link::#-audition:: plays that instead of the output so
the eq can be aimed.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
The compressor, as a UGen.

ARGUMENT:: in
The signal, any number of channels.

ARGUMENT:: name
The control the settings arrive on - fourteen numbers, see link::#-controls:: -
and the prefix of the controls around it: code::On:: (a crossfade to dry),
code::Eq::, code::EqCut:: and code::EqOn:: (the sidechain eq's bands, its two
cuts and its switch), code::Id:: and code::Meter:: (the replies a window reads).

ARGUMENT:: sidechain
A signal the detector can listen to instead of the input, or nil.

ARGUMENT:: bypass
code::false:: leaves the code::On:: control out.

METHOD:: new
Drive a control on a node - link::Classes/FxUnit#*new::.

METHOD:: onBus
A node of its own, in place on a bus - link::Classes/FxUnit#*onBus::.

METHOD:: staticGain
The gain the computer applies to a level, in dB, before the ballistics: negative
in downward mode, positive in upward.

ARGUMENT:: inDb
ARGUMENT:: threshold
ARGUMENT:: ratio
ARGUMENT:: knee
ARGUMENT:: mode
code::\down:: or code::\up::.
ARGUMENT:: range

METHOD:: modes
code::[\down, \up]::.

METHOD:: detectors
code::[\peak, \rms]::.

METHOD:: paramNames
METHOD:: specs
The settings a preset holds, and a link::Classes/ControlSpec:: for each numeric one.

METHOD:: defaultControls
METHOD:: defName
METHOD:: synthDef
The in place synth for a channel count, with a code::scBus:: for the external
sidechain.

METHOD:: meterRate
Replies a second while a window is open. 25.

METHOD:: maxLookahead
What the delay line is sized for. 0.02.

METHOD:: rmsWindow
The rms detector's window. 0.005.

METHOD:: presetNames
code::\default::, code::\vocal::, code::'drum bus'::, code::\glue::,
code::\brickwall::, code::\pump::, code::'sidechain duck'::, code::'upward
lift'::, code::\parallel::, then yours.

METHOD:: presets
METHOD:: userPresets
METHOD:: presetSettings
METHOD:: isUserPreset
METHOD:: addPreset
METHOD:: removePreset
METHOD:: clearUserPresets
METHOD:: presetFile
METHOD:: presetStore
The presets - see link::Classes/FxPresetStore::. Yours live in
code::compressor-presets.scd:: in the support folder.

METHOD:: clipboard
METHOD:: hasClipboard

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: threshold
In dB, -60 .. 0.

METHOD:: ratio
1 .. 20.

METHOD:: knee
How many dB around the threshold the curve bends over. 0 .. 24.

METHOD:: attack
METHOD:: release
In seconds, as time constants.

METHOD:: lookahead
In seconds, up to link::#*maxLookahead::. Adds that much latency.

METHOD:: range
The most the gain is ever moved, in dB.

METHOD:: mix
How much of the compressed signal goes out, 0 .. 1.

METHOD:: gain
Makeup, in dB.

METHOD:: autoGain
Adds back half of the gain change the curve makes 20 dB past the threshold -
above it downward, below it upward. A guess a fader can finish.

METHOD:: autoGainDb
METHOD:: makeup
What auto gain adds, and the makeup the node is given.

METHOD:: mode
code::\down:: or code::\up::.

METHOD:: detector
code::\peak:: or code::\rms::.

METHOD:: link
How far the channels share one gain: 1 follows the loudest, 0 lets each go its
own way.

METHOD:: sidechain
What the detector listens to instead of the input: a bus index, a
link::Classes/Bus::, a BusManager name - followed when the bus behind it moves
- or nil for the input again. Driving a graph, code::true:: switches to the
signal handed to link::#*ar::.

METHOD:: external
Whether it is listening to that.

METHOD:: sidechainName
METHOD:: sidechainLabel

METHOD:: eq
The sidechain link::Classes/ParaEQ::. Its bands and its own code::enabled::
travel through this compressor's node.

METHOD:: audition
Hear what the detector hears instead of the output. Never saved.

METHOD:: set
METHOD:: get
A setting by name.

METHOD:: staticGain
The curve with this compressor's settings.

METHOD:: meter
Whether the node reports levels. A window turns it on while open.

METHOD:: inLevel
METHOD:: outLevel
METHOD:: detLevel
Amplitudes from the last reply.

METHOD:: reduction
METHOD:: reductionMin
METHOD:: reductionMax
The gain change over the last reply, in dB - the most of it in the current mode.

METHOD:: isAlive
Whether replies are arriving.

METHOD:: preset
METHOD:: presetName
METHOD:: saveAsPreset
METHOD:: copySettings
METHOD:: pasteSettings
METHOD:: copyFrom
Presets and the clipboard, the way link::Classes/ParaEQ:: has them. Where the
sidechain comes from is not part of a preset.

METHOD:: settings
METHOD:: asDict
METHOD:: fromDict
code::(enabled:, settings:)::, the settings holding every parameter and the
sidechain eq as code::eq: (enabled:, bands:, cuts:)::.

METHOD:: controls
The fourteen numbers the node is given: threshold, ratio, knee, attack, release,
lookahead, range, makeup, mode, audition, detector, external, link.

METHOD:: id
The reply id, one per instance.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
~kick = Bus.audio(s, 2);
Ndef(\kick, {
	var env = EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.001, 0.25), Impulse.ar(2));
	var sig = SinOsc.ar(XLine.ar(180, 45, 0.08)) * env * 0.5;
	Out.ar(~kick, sig ! 2);
	sig ! 2
}).play;
Ndef(\bass, {
	var sig = RLPF.ar(LFSaw.ar([55, 55.3]) * 0.2, 600, 0.3);
	Compressor.ar(sig, \comp, In.ar(~kick, 2))
}).play;

c = Compressor(Ndef(\bass), \comp);
c.gui;
c.preset = 'sidechain duck';
c.sidechain = true;              // the kick ducks the bass
c.eq.enabled = true;
c.eq.setBand(4, 3000, -24, 0.7); // the detector stops hearing the top
c.audition = true;               // what the detector hears
c.audition = false;

c.sidechain = nil;
c.mode = \up; c.threshold = -30; c.range = 12;   // the quiet tail comes up
c.mode = \down; c.range = 60;

c.free;
Ndef(\bass).clear; Ndef(\kick).clear; ~kick.free;
::
